A Proof of Theorem 1
Theorem 1. If a model is margin-consistent, then for any robustness threshold ε, there exists a threshold λ for the logit margin dout that perfectly separates non-robust samples and robust samples. Conversely, if for any robustness threshold ε, dout admits a threshold λ that perfectly separates non-robust samples from robust samples, then the model is margin-consistent.
